@startuml agent-registration
!theme plain
title Registering and starting an agent: OS account, binding with an agent-generation grant, start through the launcher

participant "Orchestrator" as O
participant "curator-dispatcher\n(service account swarma-dispatch)" as D
participant "curator-host-helper\n(root, closed op schema)" as H
participant "Broker" as B
participant "curator-host-launcher\n(root, closed launch schema)" as L
participant "Executor\n(agent OS account)" as E

O -> D: start a worker: profile dev, accounts, until end of task
D -> D: check O may start it; allocate request_id
D -> H: sudo helper  (stdin: user.create {kind: agent, label: dev-7f3, request_id})
H -> H: under the helper lock: allocate UID, ledger entry g-0193 (creating → active)
H --> D: {username: swa-dev-7f3, uid: 30412, generation: g-0193}
D -> D: sign leaf grant: subject agent:g-0193, depth 0,\nnarrowed from its own grant (chain to the root)
D -> B: bind {uid 30412, generation g-0193, label, profiles [dev],\nchain [leaf, dispatcher grant, root],\ncaller {chain [caller grant, …, root], intersection}, request_id, expires_at}
B -> B: peer is a dispatcher principal;\nledger: g-0193 active, kind agent, created by this dispatcher;\nverify both chains, every edge incl. the leaf;\nleaf within the caller intersection; revocation state readable
B --> D: binding/1 {binding_id}
D -> D: close the broker connection
D -> L: sudo launcher  (stdin: launch.start {generation g-0193, executor, plan, request_id})
L -> L: ledger: g-0193 active; executor digest approved;\nclose inherited descriptors; clear groups; drop to uid 30412
L -> E: exec the executor as uid 30412 (sanitised environment)
E -> B: fresh connection (lease flow: lease-at-launch)
D --> O: run handle (pid, generation, binding_id)
@enduml
